  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a gate-based coherent feed-forward quantum neural network (CFFQNN) simulated in Qiskit and evaluates it on balanced credit card fraud detection and Wisconsin breast cancer classification, using 7 PCA-reduced features and a 6-qubit 3-2-1 architecture. It reports 16 CNOTs for the main CFFQNN setup, accuracy of 91% on breast cancer and 85% on credit card fraud, and appendix results of 78.80% accuracy on heart disease plus MSE 0.0102 for FixedCFFQNN on student performance, but no practical quantum advantage over classical baselines is demonstrated.",
